      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: the slider actually make sense now. Now if you set it to 0, your wrist needs to have the wrist bone origin to be inside of the collider. Before 0 wasn't zero but some arbitrary small value up to tens of centimeters. But the change is enacted retroactively to all existing worlds, so the grab distance can change unexpectedly and break interactions in old worlds (or even new ones like Virtual Dice Party).\n\nIn Virtual Dice Party worlds tabletop games which have cards are impossible to play. Cards have colliders which are like 1mm thin, distance grab is set to 0, so you need to place the root of your wrist bone EXACTLY inside of the card collider, which is basically impossible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
